---
title: Baked Chicken Thighs
source: direct-input
servings: 7
cook time: 40 to 50 minutes
---

Take your boneless, skinless @chicken thighs{1.78%lb}.

Remove any extra flaps of skin or fat.

Clean the chicken by washing it with a mixture of a little vinegar, @salt{1/2%tsp}, and water.

Thoroughly pat the chicken dry with paper towels to remove all moisture.

Place the dried chicken thighs in a #baking dish{}.

Drizzle @oil{1%tbsp} lightly over all the chicken pieces.

Using your hands, rub the oil over the chicken to coat each piece evenly.

Generously sprinkle your mixed seasoning blend, which includes @garlic powder{1%tbsp}, @onion powder{1%tbsp}, @dry thyme{1/2%tbsp}, @ground black pepper{1%tsp}, @paprika{1/2%tbsp}, @dry parsley{1/2%tbsp}, @creole seasoning{1%tbsp}, and @adobo seasoning{1/2%tbsp} over all sides of the chicken thighs. Rub it in to ensure even coverage.

> Marinate the chicken for at least 30 minutes at room temperature to allow the flavors to absorb. For deeper flavor, you can marinate it covered in the refrigerator overnight.

Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).

Place the baking dish with the chicken in the preheated oven.

Bake for ~{40-50%minutes}, or until the chicken is fully cooked through, the outside is nicely browned, and the juices run clear.

Let the chicken rest for a few minutes after baking.

Serve immediately. The chicken will be juicy on the inside with a deliciously seasoned, slightly crispy exterior.